# Copyright header

## Year (always current)

- Use the **current calendar year** in `Copyright (c) YYYY`.
- **New files**: add the standard two-line notice with that year.
- **Touched / edited files**: if the file already has the Mogu `Copyright (c) … The Mogu Authors.` line, **update `YYYY` to the current year** as part of the same change. Do not leave a past year after you modify the file.
- **Touched files with no Mogu header**: if you edit a **new engineering** file (GN, bat, skills, docs/build, `.cursor/rules` `.mdc`) that does not yet include that notice, **add the full two-line header** (current year) in the same change. Place it at the very top; for scripts that start with a shebang (`#!`), put the header **immediately after** the shebang line. For Cursor `.mdc` files, put the HTML comment block **immediately after** the YAML frontmatter.
- **Do not** copy a stale year from another file.
- **Do not** rewrite 2010–2013 product copyrights under `branches/` to Mogu Authors.

## C/C++ (`//` comments)

```cpp
// Copyright (c) YYYY The Mogu Authors.
// All rights reserved.
```

## Other languages

Same two-line text using the language’s comment syntax (e.g. `#` for Python/shell, `REM` for `.bat`, `<!-- -->` for Markdown / `.mdc`).
